  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_4bef12b2290940219a283aaabe23ad7e",
      "statement": "config.Load (internal/config/config.go) resolves configuration from three layered sources — CLI flags, environment variables, and an optional YAML config file passed via --config-file — with CLI flags overriding environment variables and environment variables overriding the config file for any setting available from more than one source.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/server/main.go#L70-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e8e12588abe930d549e13347cd5584fdd438f9c48a6613533e90f95e2f37b41:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/config/config.go#L177-L280",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b257f2f523b9b345d197d388319d010019080596b82bd6d59dbd06b8346202a9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d4b1066dd9f4da7abcd5c5dc900df37",
      "statement": "ROSA_TA_ALLOWED_NAMESPACES (and actions.allowed_namespaces in the config file) defaults to permissive: an empty/unset namespace allowlist makes the Kubernetes resource authorizer allow every namespaced request, so production deployments must set it explicitly to restrict access.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/authorization/authorization.go",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:1d35c03c15bcb3efad48a05ae2849e9a101ae157b580279029e6ec924d35b24b"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/config/config.go#L103-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a5e8ca88e9eae6ba7e83caa9987038f241cd0366e4e304a6aa40d7293c7a2e7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_81c8de72486f4b8985d0a08473260d0a",
      "statement": "ROSA_TA_AWS_ALLOWED_REGIONS (and actions.aws_allowed_regions) has no built-in non-empty default — config.Load falls back to authorization.DefaultAllowedRegions, an empty slice — causing the AWS authorizer to deny every AWS request, and cmd/server/main.go refuses to start the server at all (logger.Fatal) if the resolved allowlist is empty after config.Load runs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/server/main.go#L251-L260",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c62d9cc3ab9cb55f5c20d532864d8fc5cc6e4fb14a5611e0a2558892cb26e6ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/authorization/aws.go#L18-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4fd293f4a4967419b6dc0521c1d5fa99d39c021b2e5a774609cc280f7b002f94:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/config/config.go#L188-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf4aff0fa7efe0eea4773f3a0d04b4d2fd6c339f11cb48ce3d9b78a901a9bccf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_73dcd5fa54214af988945539686780ab",
      "statement": "ROSA_TA_AWS_ALLOWED_OPERATIONS (and actions.aws_allowed_operations) has no built-in default either, but its empty state only denies writes (reboot/terminate) while still permitting reads in allowed regions; it is not a startup failure, and cmd/server/main.go logs a warning whenever any write operation is enabled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/server/main.go#L262-L273",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00c2677f394d926d6036c7595fb18a368a66b187c578cf521458546ea8ab5cb8:"
